  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Conflict Displaced Populations in White Nile State, and Al Jazira State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to address the immediate shelter and non-food item, WASH and CCCM needs of over 94,000 newly displaced IDPs and refugees into White Nile and Al Jazira State. In White Nile State, 440 refugee households (HH) will be assisted with in-kind shelter, to alleviate the impacts of the secondary movement into the most affected localities. The project also aims to provide 10,900 personal hygiene kits and emergency wash, sanitation and hygiene engagements for 30,000 refugees in these localities. Finally, in Al Jazira state 1,200 IDP HH, and 300 refugee HH are assisted with NFI kits.</narrative>
  </description>
